# To the background and back (on the Mac = minimize then restore; on iOS = the same scene events as DM_TEST_BG): after returning the run is still there, the player can move, no red markers
# Pending version of dm/verify/scenarios/background.scn with the present-time checks (S3D-1): after the return, present readings come back
# (perf blind=false) and Frame Drops does not step down (no scale3d lv=1; DM_TEST_Q3D=0 turns the controller on). The first perf window after the
# return still holds frames from before it, so the log step separates the two expects. On ios-mac the iOS background save wait discards presents,
# and the unfixed lookup reads "no reading" from then on: RED there by design until the fix. The fix applies this file's added lines (the
# comment pair made English, env, the perf expects and the scale3d check: diff the two) to background.scn rather than copying this file over it,
# so edits made to background.scn in the meantime survive. Parse-checked by the host suite (dm/host/tests/Makefile), not run by the gate.
name background
save warlock
timeout 180
env DM_TEST_Q3D=0

enter_game
background for=3
stick 1 0 frames=30
expect_state in_game=true dead=false
expect perf timeout=25
log skip the first window after returning: it still holds frames from before the background
expect perf blind=false timeout=25
quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check no_event scale3d lv=1
